        "original_id": "73a914b5-4e4f-59f8-a790-7eedfd0d6aae",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Eleutherococcus, Amaryllis, Chengiopanax sciadophylloides\n- Taxonomy: Araliaceae, Amaryllidinae, Amaryllideae, genus classification, ITS sequence data\n\nFacts:\n- Eleutherococcus is a genus of 38 species of thorny shrubs and trees in the family Araliaceae.\n- Amaryllis is the only genus in the subtribe Amaryllidinae of the tribe Amaryllideae.\n- Chengiopanax sciadophylloides was previously included in the genus Eleutherococcus.\n- Chengiopanax sciadophylloides differs from Eleutherococcus because it does not have spines or prickles.\n- ITS sequence data confirmed the taxonomic separation of Chengiopanax sciadophylloides from Eleutherococcus.",
